 has lost.","conflict":"Gao argues the rule cannot bind his school when the bearer is disowned, while Lin's shame has made her reluctant to let the tally stand on its own terms.","outcome":"Lin's candid admission removes the concealed doubt from the record, and Mei's testimony confirms the tally was properly presented. The Crane Sect rules that its obligation does not depend on Lin's rank.","depends_on":["scn_challenge_recorded"]},{"id":"scn_lawful_loss","title":"A Victory That Would Starve","summary":"With the ruling established, Gao faces the choice beneath his challenge: accept the covenant and send an envoy, or pursue a victory that would leave his school in conflict and the rookery's cranes without protection. He recognizes that his pride has disguised fear for his school as certainty.","location_id":"loc_bannerhall","character_ids":["chr_lin_wei","chr_gao_ren"],"goal":"Gao seeks a way to protect his school's future without surrendering its claim through an unlawful breach.","conflict":"The ruling defeats his attempt to void the tally, but accepting it means attending a moot that could preserve the nesting ban.","outcome":"Gao accepts the lawful loss of his challenge and agrees to send an Eel School envoy, choosing a chance to argue for his school at the moot over a starving victory won by breaking the pact.","depends_on":["scn_tally_testimony"]},{"id":"scn_moot_convened","title":"Three Names Answer","summary":"On Saltmarket Isle, Mei opens the envoys' book as Lin presents the tally to the gathered representatives of the Crane Sect, Eel School, and Salt Wardens. The three named parties answer its summons and the peace moot is formally convened.","location_id":"loc_saltmarket_isle","character_ids":["chr_lin_wei","chr_gao_ren","chr_mei_sura"],"goal":"Lin seeks to turn the tally's binding promise into an actual moot, while Gao seeks a lawful hearing for the Eel School's needs.","conflict":"The factions remain divided over the rookery rights, and Gao must speak for his hungry school without dismissing the nesting ban.","outcome":"Mei certifies the three responses, and Gao presents his school's need to the moot rather than trying to void it. The parties begin negotiating the rookery's future under the market peace.","depends_on":["scn_lawful_loss"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"Feathers Over the Mist","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_moot_terms","title":"Room for the Eels and the Cranes","summary":"At the continuing moot on Saltmarket Isle, Gao argues for his school's survival without demanding nets within sight of nesting cranes. Mei keeps the discussion anchored to the recorded covenant, and Lin lets the tally speak without claiming a rank she no longer has.","location_id":"loc_saltmarket_isle","character_ids":["chr_lin_wei","chr_gao_ren","chr_mei_sura"],"goal":"Find terms that let the sects address the Eel School's hunger while preserving the nesting ban.","conflict":"The old rights dispute remains unresolved, and neither side can erase the cost the ban places on the Eel School.","outcome":"The moot keeps the nesting ban in force while the factions continue lawful negotiations over fishing rights beyond the nesting grounds. The immediate threat of nets at the rookery recedes.","depends_on":["scn_moot_convened"]},{"id":"scn_cranes_return","title":"The Rookery in Quiet","summary":"Lin and Gao return to the Mist Rookery after the moot begins its work. Cranes settle over the shallows without nets below them; Gao watches rather than pretending his school's hunger has vanished, and Lin no longer hides the disowning that once made her doubt her own vows.","location_id":"loc_mist_rookery","character_ids":["chr_lin_wei","chr_gao_ren"],"goal":"See whether the moot's first consequence holds at the nesting grounds and face what remains unsettled.","conflict":"The rookery is safe for now, but the Eel School still needs a durable answer and the old rivalry has not disappeared.","outcome":"Gao honors the covenant while negotiations continue, and Lin accepts that keeping her master's vow mattered more than being recognized as his student. The cranes remain above the mist as a fragile sign of peace.","depends_on":["scn_moot_terms"]}]}]}
