{"world_id":"wld_crane_banner_coast","title":"Feathers Over the Mist","logline":"Before midsummer, disowned sword-student Lin Wei must present her late master's tally to the Crane Sect, the Eel School, and the Salt Wardens and convene a peace moot, while proud Eel senior Gao Ren seeks to void it and claim the nesting shallows before the last cranes are driven away.","theme":"A vow's worth lies in keeping it, not in the rank of the one who carries it.","acts":[{"id":"act_setup","title":"The Stick and the Vow","purpose":"setup","scenes":[{"id":"scn_tally_at_dojo","title":"The Master's Last Cut","summary":"At Thunder Reed Dojo, Lin Wei studies the tally-stick her dying master entrusted to her. She sets out to deliver it before midsummer, but hides that the Crane Sect disowned her, fearing the truth will make the tally seem worthless.","location_id":"loc_thunder_reed_dojo","character_ids":["chr_lin_wei"],"goal":"Begin the journey with the tally intact and carry out her master's last order.","conflict":"Lin's shame makes her doubt that anyone will honor a vow carried by a disowned student.","outcome":"She leaves for Bannerhall with the tally, still concealing her disowning."},{"id":"scn_bannerhall_claim","title":"A Claim Beneath the Banner","summary":"At Bannerhall, Lin presents the tally to the Crane Sect. Gao Ren arrives from the Eel School and argues that her disowning voids its authority; he presses to invalidate it before it can summon a moot.","location_id":"loc_bannerhall","character_ids":["chr_lin_wei","chr_gao_ren"],"goal":"Lin seeks the Crane Sect's acknowledgment that the tally binds its named recipients.","conflict":"Gao pursues his goal of discrediting the tally, while Lin's concealment leaves her unable to answer his claim plainly.","outcome":"The Crane Sect records the dispute but will not decide it without a formal challenge witnessed under the pact. Lin must carry the tally onward, and Gao insists on contesting it lawfully.","depends_on":["scn_tally_at_dojo"]},{"id":"scn_market_filing","title":"The Envoys' Book","summary":"Lin brings the tally to Saltmarket Isle. Mei Sura registers it in the envoys' book, but asks Lin to state her standing precisely before she can certify that the market peace protects the filing.","location_id":"loc_saltmarket_isle","character_ids":["chr_lin_wei","chr_mei_sura"],"goal":"Secure a lawful record of the tally and safe conduct for its delivery to the Eel School.","conflict":"Lin's fear of rejection tempts her to keep hiding her disowning, while Mei's caution prevents her from certifying an incomplete account.","outcome":"Lin admits she is disowned. Mei records the fact alongside the tally rather than suppressing either, giving Lin a lawful filing but leaving its force contested.","depends_on":["scn_bannerhall_claim"]}]},{"id":"act_rising_action","title":"The Nesting Ban","purpose":"rising_action","scenes":[{"id":"scn_rookery_claim","title":"Shallows Without Nets","summary":"At the Mist Rookery, Lin presents the tally to Gao. Cranes circle above the nesting islets as Gao argues that his hungry school cannot endure another season without the eel grounds.","location_id":"loc_mist_rookery","character_ids":["chr_lin_wei","chr_gao_ren"],"goal":"Lin seeks Gao's acknowledgment that the Eel School is named and bound to send an envoy.","conflict":"Gao wants the tally void and the fishing rights secured, but the nesting ban forbids nets while cranes nest.","outcome":"Gao refuses to accept the tally's authority and demands a formal challenge at Bannerhall rather than breaking the covenant. Lin leaves with the dispute unresolved and the rookery still protected.","depends_on":["scn_market_filing"]},{"id":"scn_mei_stakes_neutrality","title":"A Neutral Hand","summary":"Back on Saltmarket Isle, Lin asks Mei to carry the recorded filing to Bannerhall as evidence. Mei sees that both sects are pressuring her to bend the record and chooses to stake her neutrality on its accuracy.","location_id":"loc_saltmarket_isle","character_ids":["chr_lin_wei","chr_mei_sura"],"goal":"Get the tally's complete filing before the Crane Sect so the challenge can be heard lawfully.","conflict":"Mei fears that taking a side will endanger the market's neutrality, while silence would leave Lin's admission and filing open to distortion.","outcome":"Mei agrees to bring the envoys' book herself, making the recorded facts available for the formal hearing.","depends_on":["scn_rookery_claim"]},{"id":"scn_challenge_recorded","title":"The Challenge Entered","summary":"At Bannerhall, Gao formally challenges the tally's force before the Crane Sect witnesses. Mei presents the market record, but Gao's pride makes him treat the filing as a contest of standing rather than a question of the pact's words.","location_id":"loc_bannerhall","character_ids":["chr_lin_wei","chr_gao_ren","chr_mei_sura"],"goal":"Gao seeks a witnessed ruling that will void the tally; Lin seeks a hearing that honors its terms.","conflict":"The challenge is lawful, but Gao's pride clouds his judgment, and Lin still fears that admitting her disowning will make the hearing collapse into a verdict on her worth.","outcome":"The Crane Sect accepts the formal challenge and orders both sides to answer the tally's recorded terms. No duel is fought yet; the hearing is set to continue under the covenant.","depends_on":["scn_mei_stakes_neutrality"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Word on the Stick","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_tally_testimony","title":"No Rank in the Grain","summary":"Before the witnesses at Bannerhall, Lin states plainly that she was disowned and that she kept every vow her master placed in her care. Mei reads the filing, and the Crane Sect recites the pact's rule that a presented tally obliges every named sect to send an envoy.","location_id":"loc_bannerhall","character_ids":["chr_lin_wei","chr_gao_ren","chr_mei_sura"],"goal":"Lin seeks a ruling on the tally's binding force without pretending to hold a rank she has lost.","conflict":"Gao argues the rule cannot bind his school when the bearer is disowned, while Lin's shame has made her reluctant to let the tally stand on its own terms.","outcome":"Lin's candid admission removes the concealed doubt from the record, and Mei's testimony confirms the tally was properly presented. The Crane Sect rules that its obligation does not depend on Lin's rank.","depends_on":["scn_challenge_recorded"]},{"id":"scn_lawful_loss","title":"A Victory That Would Starve","summary":"With the ruling established, Gao faces the choice beneath his challenge: accept the covenant and send an envoy, or pursue a victory that would leave his school in conflict and the rookery's cranes without protection. He recognizes that his pride has disguised fear for his school as certainty.","location_id":"loc_bannerhall","character_ids":["chr_lin_wei","chr_gao_ren"],"goal":"Gao seeks a way to protect his school's future without surrendering its claim through an unlawful breach.","conflict":"The ruling defeats his attempt to void the tally, but accepting it means attending a moot that could preserve the nesting ban.","outcome":"Gao accepts the lawful loss of his challenge and agrees to send an Eel School envoy, choosing a chance to argue for his school at the moot over a starving victory won by breaking the pact.","depends_on":["scn_tally_testimony"]},{"id":"scn_moot_convened","title":"Three Names Answer","summary":"On Saltmarket Isle, Mei opens the envoys' book as Lin presents the tally to the gathered representatives of the Crane Sect, Eel School, and Salt Wardens. The three named parties answer its summons and the peace moot is formally convened.","location_id":"loc_saltmarket_isle","character_ids":["chr_lin_wei","chr_gao_ren","chr_mei_sura"],"goal":"Lin seeks to turn the tally's binding promise into an actual moot, while Gao seeks a lawful hearing for the Eel School's needs.","conflict":"The factions remain divided over the rookery rights, and Gao must speak for his hungry school without dismissing the nesting ban.","outcome":"Mei certifies the three responses, and Gao presents his school's need to the moot rather than trying to void it. The parties begin negotiating the rookery's future under the market peace.","depends_on":["scn_lawful_loss"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"Feathers Over the Mist","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_moot_terms","title":"Room for the Eels and the Cranes","summary":"At the continuing moot on Saltmarket Isle, Gao argues for his school's survival without demanding nets within sight of nesting cranes. Mei keeps the discussion anchored to the recorded covenant, and Lin lets the tally speak without claiming a rank she no longer has.","location_id":"loc_saltmarket_isle","character_ids":["chr_lin_wei","chr_gao_ren","chr_mei_sura"],"goal":"Find terms that let the sects address the Eel School's hunger while preserving the nesting ban.","conflict":"The old rights dispute remains unresolved, and neither side can erase the cost the ban places on the Eel School.","outcome":"The moot keeps the nesting ban in force while the factions continue lawful negotiations over fishing rights beyond the nesting grounds. The immediate threat of nets at the rookery recedes.","depends_on":["scn_moot_convened"]},{"id":"scn_cranes_return","title":"The Rookery in Quiet","summary":"Lin and Gao return to the Mist Rookery after the moot begins its work. Cranes settle over the shallows without nets below them; Gao watches rather than pretending his school's hunger has vanished, and Lin no longer hides the disowning that once made her doubt her own vows.","location_id":"loc_mist_rookery","character_ids":["chr_lin_wei","chr_gao_ren"],"goal":"See whether the moot's first consequence holds at the nesting grounds and face what remains unsettled.","conflict":"The rookery is safe for now, but the Eel School still needs a durable answer and the old rivalry has not disappeared.","outcome":"Gao honors the covenant while negotiations continue, and Lin accepts that keeping her master's vow mattered more than being recognized as his student. The cranes remain above the mist as a fragile sign of peace.","depends_on":["scn_moot_terms"]}]}]}
