ojo"]},{"id":"scn_market_filing","title":"The Envoys' Book","summary":"Lin brings the tally to Saltmarket Isle. Mei Sura registers it in the envoys' book, but asks Lin to state her standing precisely before she can certify that the market peace protects the filing.","location_id":"loc_saltmarket_isle","character_ids":["chr_lin_wei","chr_mei_sura"],"goal":"Secure a lawful record of the tally and safe conduct for its delivery to the Eel School.","conflict":"Lin's fear of rejection tempts her to keep hiding her disowning, while Mei's caution prevents her from certifying an incomplete account.","outcome":"Lin admits she is disowned. Mei records the fact alongside the tally rather than suppressing either, giving Lin a lawful filing but leaving its force contested.","depends_on":["scn_bannerhall_claim"]}]},{"id":"act_rising_action","title":"The Nesting Ban","purpose":"rising_action","scenes":[{"id":"scn_rookery_claim","title":"Shallows Without Nets","summary":"At the Mist Rookery, Lin presents the tally to Gao. Cranes circle above the nesting islets as Gao argues that his hungry school cannot endure another season without the eel grounds.","location_id":"loc_mist_rookery","character_ids":["chr_lin_wei","chr_gao_ren"],"goal":"Lin seeks Gao's acknowledgment that the Eel School is named and bound to send an envoy.","conflict":"Gao wants the tally void and the fishing rights secured, but the nesting ban forbids nets while cranes nest.","outcome":"Gao refuses to accept the tally's authority and demands a formal challenge at Bannerhall rather than breaking the covenant. Lin leaves with the dispute unresolved and the rookery still protected.","depends_on":["scn_market_filing"]},{"id":"scn_mei_stakes_neutrality","title":"A Neutral Hand","summary":"Back on Saltmarket Isle, Lin asks Mei to carry the recorded filing to Bannerhall as evidence. Mei sees that both sects are pressuring her to bend the record and chooses to stake her neutrality on its accuracy.","location_id":"loc_saltmarket_isle","character_ids":["chr_lin_wei","chr_mei_sura"],"goal":"Get the tally's complete filing before the Crane Sect so the challenge can be heard lawfully.","conflict":"Mei fears that taking a side will endanger the market's neutrality, while silence would leave Lin's admission and filing open to distortion.","outcome":"Mei agrees to bring the envoys' book herself, making the recorded facts available for the formal hearing.","depends_on":["scn_rookery_claim"]},{"id":"scn_challenge_recorded","title":"The Challenge Entered","summary":"At Bannerhall, Gao formally challenges the tally's force before the Crane Sect witnesses. Mei presents the market record, but Gao's pride makes him treat the filing as a contest of standing rather than a question of the pact's words.","location_id":"loc_bannerhall","character_ids":["chr_lin_wei","chr_gao_ren","chr_mei_sura"],"goal":"Gao seeks a witnessed ruling that will void the tally; Lin seeks a hearing that honors its terms.","conflict":"The challenge is lawful, but Gao's pride clouds his judgment, and Lin still fears that admitting her disowning will make the hearing collapse into a verdict on her worth.","outcome":"The Crane Sect accepts the formal challenge and orders both sides to answer the tally's recorded terms. No duel is fought yet; the hearing is set to continue under the covenant.","depends_on":["scn_mei_stakes_neutrality"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Word on the Stick","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_tally_testimony","title":"No Rank in the Grain","summary":"Before the witnesses at Bannerhall, Lin states plainly that she was disowned and that she kept every vow her master placed in her care. Mei reads the filing, and the Crane Sect recites the pact's rule that a presented tally obliges every named sect to send an envoy.","location_id":"loc_bannerhall","character_ids":["chr_lin_wei","chr_gao_ren","chr_mei_sura"],"goal":"Lin seeks a ruling on the tally's binding force without pretending to hold a rank she